      "value": "Until now, people didn't say \"I love it\" or \"I hate it\" as much as they do now, and they didn't \"pay attention\" to the sound of the shutter in the first place. It was \"zero\". (Neutral, too.)\nWhen sound accompanies frequent and very everyday behaviors, it should be as \"zero\" as possible.\nThere is no need to try to promote or inhibit those behaviors; they should only play a minimal role.\nThere is no need to insist on their existence to people.\nIn that respect, the previous sound was appropriate.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
